ing-focused investors who want a token that grows stronger with activity and offers increasing pressure as it progresses. 2. Ethereum ($ETH) Ethereum remains the largest staking asset in crypto and still dominates validator demand going into 2026. The price sits around $2,952.40 with a daily range between $2,862.84 and $2,973.89 . Its market cap stands at $356.4B with more than $23B in 24-hour trading volume, showing how active the network remains even during slow market periods. ETH’s circulating supply is 120.6M , and since the shift to Proof of Stake , staking rewards have become a key driver for long-term holders. Millions of ETH continue to be locked in validators, giving the asset predictable demand from both retail and institutions. 3. Solana ($SOL) Solana continues to attract buyers thanks to fast transactions, active validators, and steady staking rewards. The price is currently around $139.14 , and the 24-hour range sits between $133.76 and $140.11 . With a market cap of $77.8B and more than $4.7B in daily trading volume, Solana shows strong on-chain activity. Its circulating supply sits at 559.2M , with a total supply of 614.7M . After recovering from earlier volatility, Solana’s consistent performance and large liquidity pools make it one of the most watched staking tokens heading into 2026. 4. Cardano ($ADA) Cardano maintains its position as one of the most widely used staking coins, supported by long-term holders and steady network upgrades. The price stands at $0.423 with a daily range between $0.4065 and $0.428 . ADA’s market cap is $15.48B , and trading volume sits around $791M in the last 24 hours. With a circulating supply of 36.6B ADA and a total supply capped at 45B , Cardano remains one of the largest Proof of Stake networks in the market. Because it’s easy for retail traders to stake ADA without technical hurdles, participation remains strong. Cardano keeps a stable momentum even during downturns, making it a long-term staking pick. 5. Polkadot ($DOT) Polkadot offers a staking model built around nominated validators and continues to serve as a major multi-chain hub. The price is at $2.29 with a daily range between $2.19 and $2.34 . DOT holds a market cap of $3.75B and maintains $189M in 24-hour trading volume. Its circulating supply is 1.63B DOT , matching the total supply since the network uses an inflationary model instead of a fixed cap. Traders often stake DOT to secure consistent returns and support parachain activity. The network’s interoperability design brings new activity to the ecosystem, and staking helps secure the constant flow of projects. How Noomez Coin Builds Long-Term Strength Through Its Staking System Noomez ties its story to a very clear staking design. The total supply is fixed at 280 billion $NNZ , with 140 billion sold across the 28-stage presale and no minting at launch. During the sale, buyers can lock their tokens into Noom Rewards , a presale staking pool that pays up to 66% APY with a 2x multiplier for Stage 1–7 stakers. Rewards accrue through the entire sale, then unlock 30 days after launch , which keeps early holders motivated to stay in. Fixed supply, no inflation at launch Staking rewards funded from the Noom Stake allocation Early stakers in Stage 5 still qualify for boosted terms After launch, the Keeper’s Path opens with flexible locks from 30 to 365 days , and extra rewards can flow in from the Noom Engine as partner tokens drop directly to holders. Buyers can also stack bonuses with the active BONUS250 code offering a 250% boost and a 10% referral reward . With Stage 5 live at $0.0000230 and every next stage priced higher, traders who want the strongest staking setup are moving before the later, more expensive rounds. For More Information: Website: Visit the Official Noomez Website Telegram: Join the Noomez Telegram Channel Twitter: Follow Noomez ON X (Formerly Twitter) Disclaimer: This is a sponsored press release for informational purposes only. It does not reflect the views of Times Tabloid, nor is it intended to be used as legal, tax, investment, or financial advice. Times Tabloid is not responsible for any financial losses. The post Best Cryptocurrencies to Invest In 2025: A Ranking of Top Staking Tokens Featuring NNZ Token appeared first on Times Tabloid .', 'KEYWORDS': 'Finance|News', 'LANG': 'EN', 'UPVOTES': 0, 'DOWNVOTES': 0, 'SCORE': 0, 'SENTIMENT': 'POSITIVE', 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'CREATED_ON': 1764250295, 'UPDATED_ON': None, 'SOURCE_DATA': {'TYPE': '120', 'ID': 67, 'SOURCE_KEY': 'timestabloid', 'NAME': 'TimesTabloid', 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/67/default.png', 'URL': 'https://timestabloid.com/feed/', 'LANG': 'EN', 'SOURCE_TYPE': 'RSS', 'LAUNCH_DATE': None, 'SORT_ORDER': 0, 'BENCHMARK_SCORE': 0, 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'LAST_UPDATED_TS': 1764250973, 'CREATED_ON': 1664381507, 'UPDATED_ON': 1673235440}, 'CATEGORY_DATA': [{'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 3, 'NAME': 'ADA', 'CATEGORY': 'ADA'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 21, 'NAME': 'DOT', 'CATEGORY': 'DOT'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 37, 'NAME': 'MARKET', 'CATEGORY': 'MARKET'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 50, 'NAME': 'TRADING', 'CATEGORY': 'TRADING'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 211, 'NAME': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY', 'CATEGORY': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY'}]}, {'TYPE': '121', 'ID': 54992327, 'GUID': 'https://bitcoinworld.co.in/?p=223687', 'PUBLISHED_ON': 1764250210, 'PUBLISHED_ON_NS': None, 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/82/default.png', 'TITLE': 'The Graph Price Prediction 2025-2030: Will GRT Skyrocket or Stumble?', 'SUBTITLE': None, 'AUTHORS': 'Sofiya', 'URL': 'https://bitcoinworld.co.in/the-graph-price-prediction-2030/', 'SOURCE_ID': 82, 'BODY': 'BitcoinWorld The Graph Price Prediction 2025-2030: Will GRT Skyrocket or Stumble? Are you wondering if The Graph (GRT) is poised for massive growth in the coming years? As one of the most critical infrastructure projects in the Web3 ecosystem, The Graph has captured the attention of serious cryptocurrency investors. This comprehensive The Graph price prediction analysis examines whether GRT price will surge to new heights or face challenges ahead. What is The Graph and Why Does It Matter? The Graph serves as the backbone of decentralized data querying for blockchain applications. Think of it as the Google of Web3 – it enables developers to efficiently access and process blockchain data without running their own nodes. This revolutionary approach to blockchain indexing has positioned The Graph as essential infrastructure for the entire decentralized ecosystem. The Graph Price Prediction 2025: Building Momentum Our analysis suggests 2025 could be a transformative year for GRT price. Several factors support this optimistic cryptocurrency prediction: Increased adoption of decentralized applications requiring efficient data querying Growing institutional interest in Web3 infrastructure projects Potential market recovery and broader cryptocurrency bull cycle Continued development and upgrades to The Graph network GRT Price Analysis: Technical and Fundamental Factors Understanding GRT price movements requires examining both technical indicators and fundamental value drivers. The Graph’s unique position in blockchain indexing gives it a competitive advantage that could significantly impact its long-term price trajectory. Year Conservative Prediction Moderate Prediction Optimistic Prediction 2025 $0.35 $0.65 $1.20 2026 $0.50 $0.95 $1.80 2030 $1.25 $2.50 $5.00 Blockchain Indexing Revolution: The Graph’s Competitive Edge The Graph’s approach to blockchain indexing represents a fundamental shift in how decentralized applications access data. By creating a decentralized marketplace for data queries, The Graph eliminates single points of failure and creates a more robust Web3 infrastructure. This technological advantage could drive substantial GRT price appreciation as more projects rely on The Graph’s services. Web3 Infrastructure Growth: Fueling GRT Demand The expansion of Web3 infrastructure directly correlates with The Graph’s potential value. As more developers build decentralized applications, the demand for efficient data querying solutions increases exponentially. This creates a powerful network effect that could propel GRT price to new heights in our cryptocurrency prediction models. Risk Factors in Our The Graph Price Prediction While our analysis presents an optimistic outlook, investors should consider several risk factors that could impact GRT price: Regulatory uncertainty surrounding cryptocurrency projects Competition from alternative blockchain indexing solutions Market volatility affecting all cryptocurrency assets Technology adoption rates and developer community growth Actionable Insights for GRT Investors Based on our comprehensive The Graph price prediction analysis, here are strategic considerations for potential investors: Dollar-cost averaging to manage entry points in volatile markets Monitoring network usage metrics and developer activity Diversifying within the Web3 infrastructure sector Setting realistic profit targets based on market conditions FAQs: The Graph Price Prediction Questions Answered What is The Graph’s main use case? The Graph provides decentralized indexing and querying for blockchain data, serving as critical Web3 infrastructure for applications built on networks like Ethereum and other EVM-compatible chains. Who founded The Graph? The Graph was founded by Yaniv Tal and his team, who recognized the need for better data access in the blockchain space. How does The Graph compare to traditional data solutions? Unlike centralized alternatives, The Graph offers decentralized, reliable, and efficient data querying through its global network of indexers, curators, and delegators. What companies use The Graph? Major projects including Uniswap , Aave , and Compound utilize The Graph for their data needs, demonstrating its real-world utility. Conclusion: The Future Looks Promising for GRT Our analysis indicates that The Graph occupies a unique and essential position in the Web3 ecosystem. While short-term volatility is inevitable in cryptocurrency markets, the long-term fundamentals supporting GRT price appear strong. The growing demand for efficient blockchain indexing and Web3 infrastructure suggests that The Graph could deliver substantial returns for patient investors who believe in the future of decentralized technology. To learn more about the latest cryptocurrency prediction trends, explore our article on key developments shaping The Graph and other Web3 infrastructure projects institutional adoption. This post The Graph Price Prediction 2025-2030: Will GRT Skyrocket or Stumble? first appeared on BitcoinWorld .', 'KEYWORDS': 'Crypto News|BLOCKCHAIN|CRYPTOCURRENCY|GRT|PRICE PREDICTION|The Graph', 'LANG': 'EN', 'UPVOTES': 0, 'DOWNVOTES': 0, 'SCORE': 0, 'SENTIMENT': 'POSITIVE', 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'CREATED_ON': 1764250298, 'UPDATED_ON': None, 'SOURCE_DATA': {'TYPE': '120', 'ID': 82, 'SOURCE_KEY': 'bitcoinworld', 'NAME': 'Bitcoin World', 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/82/default.png', 'URL': 'https://bitcoinworld.co.in/feed/', 'LANG': 'EN', 'SOURCE_TYPE': 'RSS', 'LAUNCH_DATE': None, 'SORT_ORDER': 0, 'BENCHMARK_SCORE': 0, 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'LAST_UPDATED_TS': 1764250975, 'CREATED_ON': 1698066984, 'UPDATED_ON': 1747932437}, 'CATEGORY_DATA': [{'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 13, 'NAME': 'BLOCKCHAIN', 'CATEGORY': 'BLOCKCHAIN'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 37, 'NAME': 'MARKET', 'CATEGORY': 'MARKET'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 50, 'NAME': 'TRADING', 'CATEGORY': 'TRADING'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 97, 'NAME': 'GRT', 'CATEGORY': 'GRT'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 211, 'NAME': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY', 'CATEGORY': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY'}]}, {'TYPE': '121', 'ID': 54992878, 'GUID': 'https://www.cryptopolitan.com/?p=869169', 'PUBLISHED_ON': 1764250207, 'PUBLISHED_ON_NS': None, 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/43/54992878.jpeg', 'TITLE': \"Nasdaq's ISE prompts SEC to quadruple daily trading limit on BlackRock's IBIT options\", 'SUBTITLE': None, 'AUTHORS': 'Florence Muchai', 'URL': 'https://www.cryptopolitan.com/nasdaq-ise-to-4x-trading-blackrock-btc-etf/', 'SOURCE_ID': 43, 'BODY': 'Nasdaq’s International Securities Exchange (ISE) has filed a proposal with the US Securities and Exchange Commission (SEC) to increase position limits on options for BlackRock’s iShares Bitcoin Trust from 250,000 contracts to 1,000,000 contracts. The change to a higher limit is meant to allow institutional traders and market makers to establish larger positions, thereby increasing market depth and liquidity for the product. Nasdaq ISE requests exemption to eliminate limits entirely The filing also requested an exemption to eliminate limits for customized “FLEX” options that are physically delivered. According to the filing, this move would “align IBIT with other major commodity-based ETFs and help pull trading activity away from opaque over-the-counter markets.” As a key factor supporting the change, Nasdaq highlighted IBIT’s market capitalization of $86.2 billion and an average daily volume of 44.6 million shares as of September 22, 2025. BlackRock holds over $71 billion in Bitcoin. The increased options limit would allow roughly $5.3 billion, representing about 8% of that total value, which is a standard, conservative practice for large ETFs The ISE proposal is subject to SEC approval, and the public comment period runs until December 17, 2025. “IBIT is now the biggest bitcoin options market in the world by open interest,” Eric Balchunas, Senior ETF Analyst at Bloomberg, stated. Additionally, Jeff Park of Bitwise Invest Advisors stated, “At last, IBIT options is finally getting the treatment it deserves. Institutional vol is finally here.” Meanwhile, BlackRock continues to accumulate Bitcoin exposure in its in-house funds. A separate Wednesday filing revealed its Strategic Income Opportunities Portfolio increased its IBIT holdings by 14% in Q3 to $155.8 million. Investors stick around even after IBIT records monthly outflows The proposal coincides with over 2 billion monthly IBIT outflows . On-chain data shows the same wallet has fallen from a $117 billion peak to $78.4 billion, losing more than 30% of its value over the past month. “…After months of steady inflows, the outflows reflect rising caution as Bitcoin falls ~22% over the past month and 7% year-to-date,” wrote Walter Bloomberg. However, ETF analyst Eric Balchunas pushed back on the panic, stating that the majority of investors are sticking around despite the outflows. He also highlighted the collapse in short interest, ascribing plummeting IBIT short interest to traders who tend to short into strength and cover in downturns. This take was supported by trading records from last week, which surpassed $40.32 billion across the 11 US-listed spot bitcoin ETFs. BlackRock’s IBIT led the industry with $27.79 billion in trading volume, accounting for nearly 70% of the total, according to data source SoSoValue. iShares Bitcoin Trust. Sources: Sosovalue Meanwhile, on November 26, IBIT had a 1-day inflow of $42.82 million, while its cumulative inflow remains extremely large at $9.98 billion. This indicates strong long-term demand. However, daily flows have been smaller recently. The fund’s net assets stand at $33.5 billion, and it is currently holding about 665.5K BTC. The premium/discount is 0.05%, meaning IBIT is trading almost exactly in line with the real Bitcoin price, with no major gap. The orange line on the chart is Bitcoin’s price trend, while the blue bars represent daily inflows/outflows. Meanwhile, Bitcoin has risen back to the $90k threshold. According to Coinmarketcap, the coin is up 5% in the last 24 hours and is now trading at $91,254. Sign up to Bybit and start trading with $30,050 in welcome gifts', 'KEYWORDS': 'News|BlackRock|BTC|IBIT|SEC', 'LANG': 'EN', 'UPVOTES': 0, 'DOWNVOTES': 0, 'SCORE': 0, 'SENTIMENT': 'POSITIVE', 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'CREATED_ON': 1764251097, 'UPDATED_ON': 1764253652, 'SOURCE_DATA': {'TYPE': '120', 'ID': 43, 'SOURCE_KEY': 'cryptopolitan', 'NAME': 'Cryptopolitan', 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://images.cryptocompare.com/news/default/cryptopolitan.png', 'URL': 'https://www.cryptopolitan.com/feed/', 'LANG': 'EN', 'SOURCE_TYPE': 'RSS', 'LAUNCH_DATE': None, 'SORT_ORDER': 0, 'BENCHMARK_SCORE': 0, 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'LAST_UPDATED_TS': 1764250951, 'CREATED_ON': 1657730129, 'UPDATED_ON': 1681205909}, 'CATEGORY_DATA': [{'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 14, 'NAME': 'BTC', 'CATEGORY': 'BTC'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 37, 'NAME': 'MARKET', 'CATEGORY': 'MARKET'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 41, 'NAME': 'REGULATION', 'CATEGORY': 'REGULATION'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 50, 'NAME': 'TRADING', 'CATEGORY': 'TRADING'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 211, 'NAME': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY', 'CATEGORY': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY'}]}, {'TYPE': '121', 'ID': 54992257, 'GUID': '635129', 'PUBLISHED_ON': 1764250206, 'PUBLISHED_ON_NS': None, 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/13/54992257.jpeg', 'TITLE': 'Bitcoin Market Structure Weakens As BTC Endures A Dramatic Sharpe Ratio Drop – What To Know', 'SUBTITLE': None, 'AUTHORS': 'Godspower Owie', 'URL': 'https://bitcoinist.com/bitcoin-market-structure-weakens/', 'SOURCE_ID': 13, 'BODY': 'Over the past week, Bitcoin has been struggling to undergo another major rally. The ongoing downward trend has hampered several crucial on-chain metrics, as they begin to turn highly negative once again, painting a highly volatile market state. A Sign Of Fading Strength In The Bitcoin Market Bitcoin’s on-chain metrics are starting to decline alongside the ongoing pullback in the price of BTC . In a sudden shift, Bitcoin’s once-confident stride has taken on a softer, more cautious pace as the leading cryptocurrency asset experienced a notable drop in the key Sharpe Ratio metric. Alphractal, an advanced investment and on-chain data analytics platform, reported this drop in the metric, which signals a less efficient market in the short term. The drop in Sharpe Ratio is the kind of shift that does not scream, but rustles. For those tracking the market through a professional lens, Alphractal highlighted that the drop in the annualized Sharpe Ratio is an important signal to gauge the next possible market direction . BTC’s Sharpe Ratio is a metric that measures risk-adjusted performance, which is essentially how much return BTC is generating for each unit of volatility. According to the on-chain data platform, a drop in this major indicator suggests that the market has lost its efficiency, aligning with the current state of the market. Several key factors have been outlined by the platform to be responsible for this decline in the Sharpe Ratio metric. The first factor is the spike in volatility after a sequence of rapid sell-offs from big and small investors. Presently, half of the 12-month accumulated returns on BTC positions have been cleared. Furthermore, a rise in systematic risk is weakening the quality of the trend, and aggressive movements from whales and leveraged traders have increased uncertainty in the market. Historic Data Points To More Bearish Period Based on past scenarios, this recent drop could trigger more volatility in the market. Alphractal highlighted that the same signal was observed in 2019, at the peak of 2021, and during the 2022 capitulation , all of which led to more challenging periods in the short to medium term. This is a typical indication of Bitcoin entering prolonged sideways phases when the Sharpe Ratio experiences a decline. During the period, BTC faces additional corrections, and the flagship asset takes longer to regain trend efficiency. However, there is a good story underneath this current trend. Once risk is repriced and the market reorganizes, Alphractal noted that significant bull cycles have always followed these resets. In the short term, this signal appears to be bearish, while in the long term, it continues to be a natural part of building new cycles. At the time of writing, the price of Bitcoin was trading at $91,388, indicating a more than 4% increase in the past day.', 'KEYWORDS': 'Bitcoin News|Alphractal|bitcoin|bitcoin news|bitcoin price|btc|BTC news|btc price|btcusd|BTCUSDT|sharpe ratio', 'LANG': 'EN', 'UPVOTES': 0, 'DOWNVOTES': 0, 'SCORE': 0, 'SENTIMENT': 'NEGATIVE', 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'CREATED_ON': 1764250254, 'UPDATED_ON': 1764250254, 'SOURCE_DATA': {'TYPE': '120', 'ID': 13, 'SOURCE_KEY': 'bitcoinist', 'NAME': 'Bitcoinist', 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://images.cryptocompare.com/news/default/bitcoinist.png', 'URL': 'https://bitcoinist.com/feed/', 'LANG': 'EN', 'SOURCE_TYPE': 'RSS', 'LAUNCH_DATE': 1387843200, 'SORT_ORDER': 0, 'BENCHMARK_SCORE': 48, 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'LAST_UPDATED_TS': 1764250935, 'CREATED_ON': 1657730129, 'UPDATED_ON': 1711620995}, 'CATEGORY_DATA': [{'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 14, 'NAME': 'BTC', 'CATEGORY': 'BTC'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 15, 'NAME': 'BUSINESS', 'CATEGORY': 'BUSINESS'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 37, 'NAME': 'MARKET', 'CATEGORY': 'MARKET'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 50, 'NAME': 'TRADING', 'CATEGORY': 'TRADING'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 211, 'NAME': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY', 'CATEGORY': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY'}]}, {'TYPE': '121', 'ID': 54992202, 'GUID': 'https://seekingalpha.com/article/4848244-when-bitcoin-price-drops-infrastructure-players-win?utm_source=cryptocompare.com&utm_medium=referral&feed_item_type=article', 'PUBLISHED_ON': 1764250086, 'PUBLISHED_ON_NS': None, 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/50/54992202.jpeg', 'TITLE': 'When Bitcoin Price Drops, Infrastructure Players Win', 'SUBTITLE': None, 'AUTHORS': '', 'URL': 'https://seekingalpha.com/article/4848244-when-bitcoin-price-drops-infrastructure-players-win?utm_source=cryptocompare.com&utm_medium=referral&feed_item_type=article', 'SOURCE_ID': 50, 'BODY': 'Summary BitFuFu stands out for its resilient cloud mining focus and strong Q3 earnings despite recent Bitcoin volatility. BitFuFu\\'s Q3 revenue doubled YoY, driven by cloud mining and a surge in mining equipment sales, with net profit reversing last year\\'s loss. The company\\'s capital-light, flexible model and high customer retention rate position FUFU to capitalize on industry downturns and future upcycles. Compared to peers, FUFU\\'s recurring, contract-driven revenue offers more stability than rivals chasing spot Bitcoin gains; I remain bullish pending Q4 results. As someone who started investing in Bitcoin ( BTC ) as early as 2018, I’ve witnessed its price crash from around $20k to $3k, only to see it surge past $50k a few years later. That experience taught me that volatility is part of the journey, not the end of it. So I’m not worried about the recent selloff; in fact, I see it as another opportunity to buy the dip. Of course, for newcomers to the crypto world, this kind of steep drop can look terrifying. But long-time investors like me know that Bitcoin selloffs don’t just create fear; they create opportunities. When prices fall and weaker miners scale back, the smartest operators seize the moment to buy cheap power, deploy rigs, and secure customers. In other words, when coin prices drop, infrastructure players build for the long run. I wrote about BitFuFu (FUFU) a while back, and it seems the share price did go up after my analysis, but unfortunately it went down recently following the industry-wide selloffs. What I want to highlight today is I am still bullish about the company given its focus on cloud mining and better than expected Q3 earnings. What is cloud mining? Cloud mining allows people to participate in BTC mining without owning or maintaining any physical equipment. Of course you can buy mining machines at home, but they are very expensive and need constant upgrades or maintenance and consume a huge amount of electricity. Unless you live in an area with extremely low-power costs, mining from a home setup usually isn’t worth it. So instead of buying and running your own rigs, you rent mining power (hashrate) from providers like BitFuFu. The provider operates large-scale mining farms in a very low-cost electricity area and allocates a portion of its computing power to each customer, who then earns Bitcoin proportional to their contract size. Another question I often get is whether the demand for cloud mining dries up when Bitcoin’s price drops. The answer, surprisingly, is no. If you look at BitFuFu’s historical performance, you’ll notice that even during bear markets, its cloud mining business has continued to grow and remain profitable. Why? Because when prices fall, long-term believers don’t disappear — they double down. Many investors view price dips as opportunities to accumulate Bitcoin, and cloud mining offers a simple, low-friction way to keep earning BTC without additional setup costs. In down markets, the number of people buying mining contracts often increases because they see it as a way to “mine the dip” — to accumulate Bitcoin at lower costs while waiting for the next up cycle. Q3 Earnings In Q3’25, BitFuFu reported total revenue of $180.7 million, doubling YoY. The key driver was its cloud-mining business, which generated $122.9 million, up 78% from the same period a year earlier. Another line of business, which I honestly didn’t know they had, is mining equipment sales, and apparently this segment jumped from less than $1 million to $35.8 million this quarter. That shows strong institutional and retail demand for hardware, which is a leading indicator that investors are quietly expanding infrastructure in anticipation of the next upcycle. Self-mining revenue dipped slightly to $20.1 million. According to the earnings report, that is due to higher network difficulty, and the company reallocated part of its hash rate from self-mining to its more profitable cloud-mining contracts. I think this move is a very smart, adaptive move that optimizes returns without overexposing itself to market volatility. Like the company CEO said so in the earnings call, \"Collecting service fees upfront improves cash flow and creates revenue visibility through orders, which greatly mitigates the uncertainty caused by Bitcoin\\'s price volatility.\" In an environment where many miners are struggling with rising hash difficulty and shrinking margins, this kind of topline growth is pretty impressive. One caveat, though, is that Q3 earnings only cover results up to September, so they may not capture the recent Bitcoin drop. I’ll be watching the Q4 report to see if this trend holds. On the bottom line, BitFuFu delivered a net profit of $11.6 million, a sharp reversal from a $5 million loss in the same quarter last year. Adjusted EBITDA jumped nearly fourfold to $22.1 million, reflecting both higher gross margins and disciplined cost management. These aren’t just accounting wins. It shows that the company has turned topline growth into real profit. That\\'s something a lot of miners struggle to do, like Bitdeer (BTDR), which we will discuss further later. The balance sheet looks solid as well. As of Q3\\'25, BitFuFu held $254.8 million in cash and digital assets, up from $168.1 million at the end of 2024. Having that kind of cash cushion matters in a choppy market like right now. That liquidity gives the company flexibility to keep expanding capacity. Another key metric worth noting is the company’s retention rate of 118.8%. Just to give some context: in the SaaS world, any business with a retention rate above 100% is considered strong, because it means existing customers are not only staying but also spending more. This kind of expansion rate signals PMF (product-market fit) and customer satisfaction. It’s rare to see that kind of stickiness in the mining industry, where churn is usually high. One more thing I don’t think the market fully appreciates is their asset-light setup. On their latest call, management said they run their own mining facility, but they also work with partners and use their mining facilities and power resources. The key idea is, in their words, they can “access and deploy significantly more hash rate with limited capital outlay.” It’s a more flexible way to grow, especially in a bear market. Honestly, I think that is super smart, especially right now when the whole sector is cooling down. If BitFuFu wants to hit their 1 GW hash rate goal, now could actually be the best time to pick up assets and cheap power deals because prices are down in this bear market. Sometimes the best opportunities show up when everyone else is just trying to survive. But here is the bigger point. The core of cloud mining is about reliability. If you are building long term contracts with big institutional clients, what matters is not all the hype during the bull market. It is being able to deliver a stable and predictable hash rate for years. That is what keeps customers coming back, hence the high retention rate mentioned earlier, and that is what helps a company look past the short-term noise. I think BitFuFu understands this, and their approach puts them in a strong spot to benefit from this down cycle. Comparative analysis I went through three companies Q3 earnings reports, and it’s clear that not all infrastructure players operate in the same way. Riot Platforms (RIOT) is a pure self-mining play. Its entire business model revolves around owning and operating massive mining facilities in Texas. Riot reported Q3’25 revenue of around $180 million and net income of $104.5 million. Its profit is highly correlated with BTC price. Bitdeer Technologies (BTDR), on the other hand, operates a model that looks much closer to BitFuFu’s. Bitdeer runs both cloud mining solutions and self-mining, with an additional hosting and data center business. In its Q3 \\'25 results, Bitdeer reported total revenue of $169.7 million, up 174% YoY, showing remarkable topline momentum. However, even though Bitdeer revenue went up 174% YoY, it recorded a net loss of $266.7 million in Q3\\'25, compared with a loss of US$50.1 million in Q3\\'24, a substantial widening of losses! Also, what’s interesting is that Bitdeer’s strategy during the quarter was to lean into direct mining profits rather than growing the cloud-mining side. Cloud mining business fell to nearly zero during the quarter. This raises a real question: if you can\\'t stay profitable when Bitcoin was at its all-time high and now that Bitcoin prices have turned downward, what happens to their bottom line in Q4? I believe BitFuFu\\'s Q4 bottom line could come under even heavier pressure unless Bitcoin prices rebound or the company rebalances toward more stable revenue streams, like cloud mining. But it seems they have stopped the cloud mining business. Will big clients still come back? It\\'s hard to tell. Hut 8 (HUT) is at an interesting transitional state. The company is evolving from a pure miner into a more diversified computing platform, such as offering GPU services, not solely mining-hash rental. From a cloud mining perspective, Bitdeer is the best comp to BitFuFu in terms of scale and business design. Both have the capacity, customer base, and brand credibility to dominate the hash-rate rental market. The difference lies in execution: BitFuFu continues to double down on cloud-mining growth even in choppy markets. Bitdeer, at least in this quarter, pivoted capacity back to self-mining, capturing short-term BTC gains but reducing the contract-driven recurring revenue that defines cloud mining’s stability. That contrast actually strengthens BitFuFu’s position in my eyes. In a bear market like where we are right now, I’d rather own the company that’s expanding its recurring, customer-based revenue than one that’s chasing the spot price of Bitcoin. Risks Right now, BitFuFu’s cloud-mining model is definitely more defensive than running big self-mining operations, thanks to its stable, contract-based income. But it’s not risk-free. If Bitcoin keeps sliding, margins across the board get squeezed, and even cloud-mining fees could take a hit as customers rethink ROI. There’s also the question of whether BitFuFu can actually lock in cheap power deals and good assets while the market is weak. Downturns are usually the best time to pick up bargains, but they’re also when other players are hunting for the same distressed opportunities. Conclusion Like Warren Buffett used to say, when the tide goes out, you see who’s been swimming naked. When the market turns bearish, we see which businesses were built on leverage and which ones are on real operational strength. One caveat, as I mentioned earlier, is that the Q3 earnings only cover results through September and don’t capture the latest Bitcoin sell-off. I’ll be watching the Q4 report closely, and if this trend of resilience and disciplined growth continues, I plan to increase my position.', 'KEYWORDS': 'BTDR|RIOT|BTC|FUFU', 'LANG': 'EN', 'UPVOTES': 0, 'DOWNVOTES': 0, 'SCORE': 0, 'SENTIMENT': 'POSITIVE', 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'CREATED_ON': 1764250158, 'UPDATED_ON': 1764250159, 'SOURCE_DATA': {'TYPE': '120', 'ID': 50, 'SOURCE_KEY': 'seekingalpha', 'NAME': 'Seeking Alpha', 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://images.cryptocompare.com/news/default/seekingalpha.png', 'URL': 'https://seekingalpha.com/feeds/cryptocompare/cryptos', 'LANG': 'EN', 'SOURCE_TYPE': 'RSS', 'LAUNCH_DATE': None, 'SORT_ORDER': 0, 'BENCHMARK_SCORE': 0, 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'LAST_UPDATED_TS': 1764250971, 'CREATED_ON': 1657730129, 'UPDATED_ON': 1673257636}, 'CATEGORY_DATA': [{'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 14, 'NAME': 'BTC', 'CATEGORY': 'BTC'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 15, 'NAME': 'BUSINESS', 'CATEGORY': 'BUSINESS'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 37, 'NAME': 'MARKET', 'CATEGORY': 'MARKET'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 39, 'NAME': 'MINING', 'CATEGORY': 'MINING'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 211, 'NAME': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY', 'CATEGORY': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY'}]}, {'TYPE': '121', 'ID': 54992163, 'GUID': 'https://coinpaper.com/12709/bitcoin-s-cycle-isn-t-done-three-weekly-signals-suggest-a-100-rally-ahead', 'PUBLISHED_ON': 1764249990, 'PUBLISHED_ON_NS': None, 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/93/default.png', 'TITLE': 'Bitcoin’s Cycle Isn’t Done: Three Weekly Signals Suggest a 100% Rally Ahead', 'SUBTITLE': None, 'AUTHORS': '', 'URL': 'https://coinpaper.com/12709/bitcoin-s-cycle-isn-t-done-three-weekly-signals-suggest-a-100-rally-ahead', 'SOURCE_ID': 93, 'BODY': 'Bitcoin traders are tracking three long-term signals as price sits between a reclaimed support line and a crucial resistance zone. A four-year trendline flip, a key barrier near 91,000 dollars, and a weekly hidden bullish divergence together suggest the current cycle may still have room to run. BTC Reclaims 4-Year Trendline as Support Bitcoin has returned to a four-year trendline that previously acted as major resistance on the weekly BTC/USDT chart. Bitcoin 1W Multi-Year Trendline Hold. Source: TradingView / X The chart shows price holding near the diagonal line that capped rallies in 2021 and 2022 and later guided the advance into the 2024–2025 highs. Recent candles sit just above this level, marked as macro support, after the latest pullback. Crypto analyst @ardizor highlighted the move on X, writing that “$BTC is back on the 4-year trendline” and that “resistance finally turned support.” He described the structure as “mega bullish longterm,” pointing to the trendline hold as a signal that the broader uptrend remains in place despite recent volatility. Analyst Says Bitcoin Near Crucial Resistance With Path to $100K Bitcoin is approaching a key resistance zone that could reopen a path to $100,000 if it breaks, according to trader Michaël van de Poppe. His latest BTC/USDT chart shows price pushing into the first “crucial resistance zone” after a sharp rebound from recent lows. Bitcoin Crucial Resistance Zone Near $91K. Source: Michaël van de Poppe Van de Poppe wrote that he views the move as a “pretty strong bounce upwards” but wants to see consolidation below resistance before any breakout. In his view, a clean move through this band would signal that downside pressure is fading and that the market trend is turning back upward. He added that a retest near $88,000 would not surprise him and could still fit a constructive structure. However, he said that if the current level holds and breaks higher, the odds increase that Bitcoin has already set its cycle low. “The cycle is far from over,” he concluded. Bitcoin Shows Weekly Hidden Bullish Divergence, Analyst Says Meanwhile, Bitcoin printed a hidden weekly bullish divergence on the one-week BTC/USD index chart, analyst Cas Abbé wrote on X. Bitcoin Weekly Hidden Bullish Divergence. Source: X A hidden bullish divergence forms when price builds higher lows while the momentum oscillator draws lower lows. The pattern often appears during trend continuation phases, not trend reversal. Abbé connected his call to previous signals, saying the last two similar prints were followed by rallies near 100%. The chart highlights a series of higher-low ranges framed inside gold boxes, marking prior continuation swings within the broader multi-year channel. Those prior bounces, marked on the lower momentum pane, weakened temporarily yet did not invalidate the directional sequence that resumed afterward. Abbé’s note framed the signal as evidence that weekly momentum has cooled earlier without breaking trend structure. As a result, analysts widely treat the divergence as a continuation indicator when combined with a rising diagonal price floor, seen multiple times in prior cycles.', 'KEYWORDS': 'News|Bitcoin', 'LANG': 'EN', 'UPVOTES': 0, 'DOWNVOTES': 0, 'SCORE': 0, 'SENTIMENT': 'POSITIVE', 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'CREATED_ON': 1764250068, 'UPDATED_ON': None, 'SOURCE_DATA': {'TYPE': '120', 'ID': 93, 'SOURCE_KEY': 'coinpaper', 'NAME': 'Coinpaper', 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/93/default.png', 'URL': 'https://coinpaper.com/newsfeed', 'LANG': 'EN', 'SOURCE_TYPE': 'RSS', 'LAUNCH_DATE': 1646092800, 'SORT_ORDER': 0, 'BENCHMARK_SCORE': 0, 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'LAST_UPDATED_TS': 1764250976, 'CREATED_ON': 1709283963, 'UPDATED_ON': 1709284009}, 'CATEGORY_DATA': [{'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 14, 'NAME': 'BTC', 'CATEGORY': 'BTC'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 26, 'NAME': 'FIAT', 'CATEGORY': 'FIAT'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 37, 'NAME': 'MARKET', 'CATEGORY': 'MARKET'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 50, 'NAME': 'TRADING', 'CATEGORY': 'TRADING'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 211, 'NAME': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY', 'CATEGORY': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY'}]}, {'TYPE': '121', 'ID': 54992162, 'GUID': 'https://bitcoinworld.co.in/?p=223688', 'PUBLISHED_ON': 1764249911, 'PUBLISHED_ON_NS': None, 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/82/default.png', 'TITLE': 'Smart CalSTRS Investment: How This $80M MicroStrategy Move Boosts Bitcoin Exposure', 'SUBTITLE': None, 'AUTHORS': 'Editorial Team', 'URL': 'https://bitcoinworld.co.in/calstrs-investment-microstrategy-bitcoin/', 'SOURCE_ID': 82, 'BODY': 'BitcoinWorld Smart CalSTRS Investment: How This $80M MicroStrategy Move Boosts Bitcoin Exposure When the California State Teachers’ Retirement System makes a move, the financial world pays attention. The recent revelation that CalSTRS holds $80 million in MicroStrategy stock represents a significant milestone in institutional cryptocurrency adoption. This strategic CalSTRS investment demonstrates how major pension funds are positioning themselves for the digital asset revolution. Why Is the CalSTRS Investment in MicroStrategy So Important? As the third-largest pension fund in the United States, CalSTRS manages retirement assets for nearly one million California educators. Their investment decisions carry enormous weight and influence institutional investment trends. The $80 million CalSTRS investment in MicroStrategy isn’t just about stock ownership—it’s about indirect Bitcoin exposure through one of corporate America’s most vocal crypto advocates. MicroStrategy has become famous for its massive Bitcoin treasury holdings. Therefore, when CalSTRS invests in MSTR stock, they’re effectively gaining exposure to Bitcoin without directly holding the cryptocurrency. This approach allows traditional institutions to participate in crypto markets while navigating regulatory frameworks they understand. How Does This CalSTRS Investment Impact Bitcoin Adoption? The CalSTRS investment signals a crucial shift in how large institutions view digital assets. Pension funds typically follow conservative investment strategies focused on long-term stability. Their involvement suggests that Bitcoin and cryptocurrency exposure are becoming mainstream investment considerations. Consider these key implications of the CalSTRS investment strategy: Validation – Major pension funds now see crypto exposure as legitimate Accessibility – Traditional investors can gain Bitcoin exposure through regulated vehicles Trendsetting – Other pension funds may follow CalSTRS’ lead Market impact – Institutional money brings stability and liquidity What Challenges Does This CalSTRS Investment Face? While the CalSTRS investment represents progress, it also comes with unique challenges. MicroStrategy’s stock performance remains closely tied to Bitcoin price movements, creating volatility that pension funds typically avoid. However, the CalSTRS investment team appears confident that the long-term potential outweighs short-term fluctuations. Moreover, regulatory uncertainty continues to impact institutional crypto investments. The CalSTRS investment approach through MicroStrategy stock provides a workaround that complies with existing investment guidelines while still gaining cryptocurrency exposure. What Can Other Investors Learn From This CalSTRS Move? The CalSTRS investment offers valuable lessons for both institutional and individual investors. First, it demonstrates that there are multiple paths to gain cryptocurrency exposure beyond direct ownership. Second, it shows that even conservative institutions recognize the importance of digital assets in modern portfolios. Key takeaways from the CalSTRS investment strategy include: Diversified approach – Consider indirect exposure through companies like MicroStrategy Long-term perspective – Pension funds think in decades, not days Risk management – Balance innovation with established investment principles Trend awareness – Monitor how major institutions position themselves Conclusion: The Future of Institutional Crypto Investment The $80 million CalSTRS investment in MicroStrategy marks a pivotal moment in cryptocurrency adoption. It demonstrates that sophisticated institutional investors recognize the value of Bitcoin exposure and have found creative ways to incorporate it into their portfolios. As more traditional funds follow this CalSTRS investment model, we can expect increased stability and legitimacy in crypto markets. Frequently Asked Questions How much MicroStrategy stock does CalSTRS own? CalSTRS holds 448,000 shares of MicroStrategy stock valued at approximately $80 million according to BitcoinTreasuries.NET. Why would CalSTRS invest in MicroStrategy instead of buying Bitcoin directly? Investing in MicroStrategy stock allows CalSTRS to gain Bitcoin exposure through a regulated, traditional investment vehicle while navigating their established investment guidelines and regulatory framework. What percentage of CalSTRS’ portfolio is this investment? While the $80 million investment sounds substantial, it represents a small fraction of CalSTRS’ nearly $300 billion total portfolio, demonstrating a measured approach to crypto exposure. How does this investment benefit California teachers? As a pension fund, CalSTRS’ investment decisions aim to generate returns that fund retirement benefits for nearly one million California educators and their families. Are other pension funds making similar investments? While specific investments vary, many institutional investors are exploring cryptocurrency exposure through various channels, with CalSTRS being one of the most prominent examples. What risks does this investment carry? The primary risks include Bitcoin price volatility affecting MicroStrategy’s stock value and regulatory changes that could impact cryptocurrency-related investments. Found this analysis of the CalSTRS investment strategy insightful? Share this article with colleagues and investors who need to understand how institutional money is flowing into cryptocurrency markets. Your shares help spread crucial market intelligence! To learn more about the latest institutional Bitcoin adoption trends, explore our article on key developments shaping Bitcoin price action and corporate investment strategies. This post Smart CalSTRS Investment: How This $80M MicroStrategy Move Boosts Bitcoin Exposure first appeared on BitcoinWorld .', 'KEYWORDS': 'Crypto News|BITCOIN|CalSTRS|Institutional Investment|Microstrategy|Pension Funds', 'LANG': 'EN', 'UPVOTES': 0, 'DOWNVOTES': 0, 'SCORE': 0, 'SENTIMENT': 'POSITIVE', 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'CREATED_ON': 1764250067, 'UPDATED_ON': None, 'SOURCE_DATA': {'TYPE': '120', 'ID': 82, 'SOURCE_KEY': 'bitcoinworld', 'NAME': 'Bitcoin World', 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/82/default.png', 'URL': 'https://bitcoinworld.co.in/feed/', 'LANG': 'EN', 'SOURCE_TYPE': 'RSS', 'LAUNCH_DATE': None, 'SORT_ORDER': 0, 'BENCHMARK_SCORE': 0, 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'LAST_UPDATED_TS': 1764250975, 'CREATED_ON': 1698066984, 'UPDATED_ON': 1747932437}, 'CATEGORY_DATA': [{'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 14, 'NAME': 'BTC', 'CATEGORY': 'BTC'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 15, 'NAME': 'BUSINESS', 'CATEGORY': 'BUSINESS'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 37, 'NAME': 'MARKET', 'CATEGORY': 'MARKET'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 50, 'NAME': 'TRADING', 'CATEGORY': 'TRADING'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 211, 'NAME': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY', 'CATEGORY': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY'}]}, {'TYPE': '121', 'ID': 54992488, 'GUID': 'https://en.coinotag.com/blackrock-bitcoin-etf-investors-return-to-profit-amid-signs-of-december-recovery', 'PUBLISHED_ON': 1764249878, 'PUBLISHED_ON_NS': None, 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/77/54992488.jpeg', 'TITLE': 'BlackRock Bitcoin ETF Investors Return to Profit Amid Signs of December Recovery', 'SUBTITLE': None, 'AUTHORS': 'COINOTAG Editorial Team', 'URL': 'https://en.coinotag.com/blackrock-bitcoin-etf-investors-return-to-profit-amid-signs-of-december-recovery', 'SOURCE_ID': 77, 'BODY': \"BlackRock Bitcoin ETF investors have returned to profit with a cumulative gain of $3.2 billion as Bitcoin surpasses $90,000, indicating a strengthening market sentiment and potential recovery in December 2025 for this key driver of BTC's all-time highs. BlackRock's iShares Bitcoin Trust ETF (IBIT) holders flipped from losses to $3.2 billion in profits after Bitcoin's [...]\", 'KEYWORDS': 'Analysis|Bitcoin|News', 'LANG': 'EN', 'UPVOTES': 0, 'DOWNVOTES': 0, 'SCORE': 0, 'SENTIMENT': 'POSITIVE', 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'CREATED_ON': 1764250537, 'UPDATED_ON': 1764250538, 'SOURCE_DATA': {'TYPE': '120', 'ID': 77, 'SOURCE_KEY': 'coinotag', 'NAME': 'CoinOtag', 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/77/default.png', 'URL': 'https://en.coinotag.com/feed/', 'LANG': 'EN', 'SOURCE_TYPE': 'RSS', 'LAUNCH_DATE': None, 'SORT_ORDER': 0, 'BENCHMARK_SCORE': 0, 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'LAST_UPDATED_TS': 1764250991, 'CREATED_ON': 1686819961, 'UPDATED_ON': 1717748924}, 'CATEGORY_DATA': [{'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 14, 'NAME': 'BTC', 'CATEGORY': 'BTC'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 15, 'NAME': 'BUSINESS', 'CATEGORY': 'BUSINESS'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 37, 'NAME': 'MARKET', 'CATEGORY': 'MARKET'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 211, 'NAME': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY', 'CATEGORY': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY'}]}, {'TYPE': '121', 'ID': 54992487, 'GUID': 'https://en.coinotag.com/do-kwon-requests-5-year-limit-in-terra-fraud-sentencing', 'PUBLISHED_ON': 1764249679, 'PUBLISHED_ON_NS': None, 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/77/54992487.jpeg', 'TITLE': 'Do Kwon Requests 5-Year Limit in Terra Fraud Sentencing', 'SUBTITLE': None, 'AUTHORS': 'COINOTAG Editorial Team', 'URL': 'https://en.coinotag.com/do-kwon-requests-5-year-limit-in-terra-fraud-sentencing', 'SOURCE_ID': 77, 'BODY': \"Do Kwon, co-founder of Terraform Labs, has requested a five-year prison sentence in his fraud case related to the Terra ecosystem collapse, which wiped out nearly $40 billion in investor value. This plea follows his guilty admission to conspiracy and wire fraud, avoiding a full trial after extradition from Montenegro. Do Kwon's defense argues five [...]\", 'KEYWORDS': 'Analysis|News', 'LANG': 'EN', 'UPVOTES': 0, 'DOWNVOTES': 0, 'SCORE': 0, 'SENTIMENT': 'NEGATIVE', 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'CREATED_ON': 1764250536, 'UPDATED_ON': 1764250537, 'SOURCE_DATA': {'TYPE': '120', 'ID': 77, 'SOURCE_KEY': 'coinotag', 'NAME': 'CoinOtag', 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/77/default.png', 'URL': 'https://en.coinotag.com/feed/', 'LANG': 'EN', 'SOURCE_TYPE': 'RSS', 'LAUNCH_DATE': None, 'SORT_ORDER': 0, 'BENCHMARK_SCORE': 0, 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'LAST_UPDATED_TS': 1764250991, 'CREATED_ON': 1686819961, 'UPDATED_ON': 1717748924}, 'CATEGORY_DATA': [{'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 15, 'NAME': 'BUSINESS', 'CATEGORY': 'BUSINESS'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 34, 'NAME': 'LUNA', 'CATEGORY': 'LUNA'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 37, 'NAME': 'MARKET', 'CATEGORY': 'MARKET'}]}, {'TYPE': '121', 'ID': 54991936, 'GUID': 'https://u.today/dogecoin-down-80-in-etf-inflows-overnight-heres-doge-price-reaction', 'PUBLISHED_ON': 1764249600, 'PUBLISHED_ON_NS': None, 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/64/54991936.jpeg', 'TITLE': \"Dogecoin Down 80% in ETF Inflows Overnight, Here's DOGE Price Reaction\", 'SUBTITLE': None, 'AUTHORS': 'U.Today', 'URL': 'https://u.today/dogecoin-down-80-in-etf-inflows-overnight-heres-doge-price-reaction', 'SOURCE_ID': 64, 'BODY': \"Dogecoin's ETF inflows collapsed from $1.8 million to $365,420 in a single day, an 80% cut that hit sentiment fast and forced DOGE traders to react as the price tries to make it to December.\", 'KEYWORDS': 'Dogecoin ETF', 'LANG': 'EN', 'UPVOTES': 0, 'DOWNVOTE